          "text": "Associated headache symptoms and pertinent negatives"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Rare mild nausea; no vomiting, photophobia, phonophobia, aura, visual change, focal neurological symptoms, speech change, confusion, thunderclap onset, or 'worst ever' headache. No fever, neck stiffness, weight loss, night sweats, sinus symptoms, or trauma."
      }
    },
